  "id": "BIT-mongodb-2026-82063",
  "summary": "Use-After-Free in MongoDB Server Cursor Management Component Leads to Denial of Service",
  "details": "A use-after-free security issue in the cursor management component of MongoDB Server allows an authenticated user to cause a denial of service. Under specific timing conditions during cursor operations, a stale pointer to a freed resource may be retained and subsequently dereferenced during cursor cleanup, leading to a server process crash.",
